# ✅ ToDoList App

A full-featured task management web application built with **ASP.NET MVC** and **Entity Framework**. Users can register, log in, and manage their own personal tasks through a clean and responsive interface. Authentication is handled via **ASP.NET Identity**, ensuring each user only sees and manages their own data.

---

## 🚀 Features

- User registration and login with **ASP.NET Identity**
- Each user has their own private task list — no data leakage between accounts
- Create, read, update and delete tasks (full CRUD)
- Mark tasks as complete / incomplete
- Responsive UI built with Bootstrap and custom CSS
- Data persistence with SQL Server via Entity Framework
- Clean MVC architecture with separation of concerns

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Framework | ASP.NET MVC (.NET Framework) |
| Language | C# |
| Authentication | ASP.NET Identity |
| ORM | Entity Framework (Code First) |
| Database | SQL Server |
| Frontend | HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, JavaScript |

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
CodeAlpha_ToDoList/
├── Controllers/        # MVC Controllers (Tasks, Account)
├── Models/             # Entity models, Identity user, data annotations
├── Views/              # Razor views for UI (Tasks, Account, Shared)
├── Migrations/         # Entity Framework database migrations
├── Content/            # CSS stylesheets
├── Custom_Scripts/     # Custom JavaScript files
└── App_Start/          # Application configuration (routes, bundles, Identity)
```

---

## ⚙️ Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Visual Studio 2019 or later
- .NET Framework 4.7+
- SQL Server (LocalDB or full instance)

### Installation

1. **Clone the repository**
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/alaaedinne08/CodeAlpha_ToDoList.git
   cd CodeAlpha_ToDoList
   ```

2. **Configure the connection string**
   Open `Web.config` and update the connection string to point to your SQL Server instance:
   ```xml
   <connectionStrings>
     <add name="DefaultConnection"
          connectionString="Data Source=(localdb)\MSSQLLocalDB;Initial Catalog=ToDoListDb;Integrated Security=True"
          providerName="System.Data.SqlClient" />
   </connectionStrings>
   ```

3. **Apply migrations**
   Open the Package Manager Console in Visual Studio and run:
   ```
   Update-Database
   ```

4. **Run the application**
   Press `F5` in Visual Studio or use:
   ```bash
   dotnet run
   ```

5. **Register an account** and start managing your tasks.

---

## 🔐 Authentication Flow

- Built on top of **ASP.NET Identity** for secure user management
- Users register with email and password
- Passwords are hashed automatically by Identity
- Each task is linked to the authenticated user — users cannot access each other's data
- Protected routes redirect unauthenticated users to the login page via `[Authorize]` attribute

